        "text": "Each asset you have in your portfolio will have some risk associated with it. For example, a new cryptocurrency without a large market for buyers will have more liquidity risk. But the risk won't always be internal and manageable with your portfolio. Sometimes external factors, like our Lehman Brothers example or a global recession can't be avoided. So how do you begin to assess these risks, the likelihood of encountering them, and their severity? An excellent place to start is by ranking your investments from high risk to low risk. From there, you can check each asset's price, volatility, liquidity, industry health and other related news.",
